.SS FASTCALL
.IP
.EX
#define FASTCALL
#define fastcall
.EE
.PP
Requests that function arguments be passed in registers according to the
compiler\(aqs \f[B]fastcall\f[R] convention instead of entirely on the
stack.
.PP
Typical \f[B]32\-bit x86 fastcall\f[R] register usage:
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
l.
T{
Register usage (in order)
T}
_
T{
\f[CR]ECX\f[R], \f[CR]EDX\f[R]
T}
.TE
.IP \(bu 2
Register usage is \f[B]compiler\-defined\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Usually limited to \f[B]two arguments\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Remaining arguments (if any) are passed on the stack
.IP \(bu 2
Return values are unaffected
.PP
\f[B]Examples\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
int fastcall func(int a, void *b);
.EE
.IP
.EX
int FASTCALL func(int a, int b, int c, int d, int e);
.EE
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]a\f[R] \-> \f[CR]ECX\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]b\f[R] \-> \f[CR]EDX\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]c\f[R], \f[CR]d\f[R], \f[CR]e\f[R] \-> stack
.PP
Prototype:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]extern\f[R] int fastcall func(int, int, void *);
.EE
.PP
Function pointer:
.IP
.EX
int (FASTCALL *test)(int, int, void *);
.EE
.PP
Function pointer type casting:
.IP
.EX
test = (int (FASTCALL *)(int))pointer;
.EE
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS IS__FASTCALL__SUPPORTED
.IP
.EX
#define IS__FASTCALL__SUPPORTED
.EE
.PP
Checks whether the \f[CR]FASTCALL\f[R] macro is defined as non\-empty.
This indicates that the compiler truly supports the \f[CR]fastcall\f[R]
calling convention.
.RS
.PP
Note:
.PP
Checking \f[CR]IS__FASTCALL__SUPPORTED\f[R] alone is not sufficient.
.PP
You must also verify that your target architecture and compiler supports
fastcall.
.RE
.PP
Example:
.IP
.EX
#ifdef IS__FASTCALL__SUPPORTED
int FASTCALL fast_add(int a, int b);
#else
int fast_add(int a, int b);
#endif
.EE
